// ============================================================
// ZKAuction — Private Reserve Auction Smart Contract
// Language: Compact (Midnight Network's ZK smart contract DSL)
//
// ⚠️ PLACEHOLDER — Phase 0 scaffolding only.
//    Real contract logic written in Phase 1.
//
// PRIVACY MODEL (what this contract will enforce):
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// ✅ HIDDEN from observers:
//    • The reserve price (stored as a cryptographic commitment)
//    • Individual bidder identities (DApp-specific ephemeral keys)
//
// 👁️ VISIBLE on-chain:
//    • A reserve_commitment (the hash — not the price)
//    • The highest bid amount (public, so bidders know what to beat)
//    • Auction status (open / settled / expired)
//    • The winning bid amount (revealed only at settlement)
//
// KEY CONCEPTS for first-timers:
// ─────────────────────────────
// ledger { }   → public, persistent on-chain state (visible to all)
// circuit { }  → ZK-provable function (inputs are proven, not exposed)
// witness      → private input to a circuit (never leaves your device)
// disclose()   → explicitly moves data from private → public state
// ============================================================

